# Repo-root .dockerignore.
#
# The MCP image is built with context = repo root (see azure.yaml) so the
# Dockerfile can `COPY agents/ crowd/ mcp/` in one go. Docker looks for
# .dockerignore at the CONTEXT root, not next to the Dockerfile, which is
# why mcp/.dockerignore alone wasn't enough — historically the entire
# _demo_data_files/ directory (~160 MB) was uploaded to ACR Tasks on
# every deploy, making "Uploading remote build context" take many minutes
# or stall outright.
#
# Keep this list aligned with mcp/.dockerignore (kept for local
# `docker build mcp/` flows that use mcp/ as the context).

# VCS + virtualenv + caches
.git
.gitignore
.venv
.venv-*
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.tox
**/*.egg-info
.import-*
.reference-*
.import-snapshot.py
.refactor-import.py
.finish-import.py
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# IDE
.vscode
.idea
*.swp

# azd local state
.azure

# Node / Next.js artefacts (webui only — it has its own .dockerignore for its
# own build context, but listing here keeps a stray COPY * from grabbing them)
node_modules
.next
*.tsbuildinfo
webui/.next
webui/node_modules

# Large demo data + load notebooks — NOT needed inside the MCP container.
# The MCP tools query Fabric directly; these JSON dumps + ingest notebooks
# are only used by the local `_load_demo_data.ipynb` workflow.
_demo_data_files
_load_demo_data.ipynb
_create_tables.ipynb
_onto_dump.json
_gen_demo_data.py
_count_rows.py
_create_and_run_load_notebook.py
_create_and_run_tables_notebook.py
_create_load_notebook.py
_create_ontology.py
_verify_ontology.py
create_lakehouse_tables.py

# Test traces and result outputs that change frequently — never needed at
# runtime in the container.
agents/tests/results

# Local logs
*.log
logs

# Docs — exclude markdown by default, but allow the prompt files MCP
# actually reads at runtime back in via `!`.
*.md
!agents/CopilotSDK_Instructions.md
!agents/Method6_Council_Instructions.md
!agents/Method7_WorkIQ_Instructions.md
